^IBMPC 3.3 doesn't boot
Check MSDOS 7.1 boot only file list
Check MSDOS 7.1 Startup + Tools file list and correct autoexec.bat and config.sys
change .gitignore to ignore all files in the dos payload sub directories but include the directory
with a readme.txt that says to drop the .img files into the directory for vhdmaker to use
example winworldpc .7z extracted into the root of the folder.

 You can still include Freedos
and MS-DOS 1.0, MS-DOS 1.25, MS-DOS 2.0, MS-DOS 4.0 as they are now open source by Microsoft here
https://github.com/microsoft/ms-dos and here: https://github.com/DOS-History/Paterson-Listings

Add OpenDOS download and build options like FreeDOS https://github.com/the-grue/OpenDOS

Include PDOS https://github.com/Arquivotheca/PDOS

